, "source_unit": {"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "0GE6", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{proposition-spaces-diagonal-representable-noetherian}", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$F : (\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\etale^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta : F \\to F \\times F$", "MATH_0004": "$F$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_{S, s}$", "MATH_0006": "$s$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$F' : (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0009": "$(\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0010": "$F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-definition-representable-morphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proposition}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{proposition}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d6a7515d80ef8ced345104d8582163c418fff36b608363f73b199807bee7918e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3b53c7ec4e3721f5243398fbc3d3a9fd4f51197038f8fe2f9a5978cb4a4d48d0", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let\n<MATH_0002>\nbe a functor. Assume that\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is representable\n(as a transformation of functors, see\nCategories, Definition <REF_0001>),\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0004> satisfies axioms [-1], [0], [1], [2], [3], [4], [5]\n(see above), and\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0005> is a G-ring for all finite type points <MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nThen there exists a unique algebraic space\n<MATH_0008>\nwhose restriction to <MATH_0009> is <MATH_0010>\n(see proof for elucidation).\n<STRUCT_0007>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f6200ec1b35875f571e6311fe9304c3beed4e06320eba7ff6c0363c7bd0bc472", "unit_id": "inventory:artin:0GE7:proposition/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:4ca1fa30e78863fe2d82ef73f91b97d3bd2d31b483bedebca062a65491be1fa5", "hash": "sha256:4ca1fa30e78863fe2d82ef73f91b97d3bd2d31b483bedebca062a65491be1fa5", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 190615, "byte_start": 190124, "file": "artin.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:aff914bff663e22ffa390e7d6e8685b11238860ad8aed52e41ad4a1f94e44b80", "line_end": 4852, "line_start": 4844}, "owner_tag": "0GE6", "parent_tag": "0GE6", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0GE6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$x \\in F(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$u_0 \\in U$", "MATH_0006": "$x$", "MATH_0007": "$u_0$", "MATH_0008": "$u_0 \\in U' \\subset U$", "MATH_0009": "$x$", "MATH_0010": "$U'$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:591ff32965cf6fd4ec0139050cd624643f4032874de167c62f2d806a586b966b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:96ee58066ef92127d959e13387c5d5f83a43bd3651845c8c9476783c88fbe1d3", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAxiom [5]. This is the axiom stating that <MATH_0001> satisfies openness of versality.\nRecall that this means the following: Given a scheme <MATH_0002>\nlocally of finite type over <MATH_0003>, given <MATH_0004>, and given\na finite type point <MATH_0005> such that <MATH_0006> is versal at <MATH_0007>,\nthen there exists an open neighbourhood <MATH_0008>\nsuch that <MATH_0009> is versal at every finite type point of <MATH_0010>.\nAs before, verifying this only involves evaluating\nour functor at Noetherian schemes.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5a42c13ade9495138252e91f1a3d75f9d78f813a39638238c5b26b65f2353c6a", "unit_id": "inventory:artin:0GE6:paragraph/0008"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:25a092a52d09d3d52850610e4b6bdf2d3b243559d959aad11f517037610f11fc", "hash": "sha256:25a092a52d09d3d52850610e4b6bdf2d3b243559d959aad11f517037610f11fc", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 192540, "byte_start": 191384, "file": "artin.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:42eb298211cdb763448bc1c40e0d44014eb32e8bcf704e24ac2c71b4f34e7fed", "line_end": 4896, "line_start": 4873}, "owner_tag": "0GE7", "parent_tag": "0GE6", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0GE6", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$F' : (\\Sch/S)_\\etale^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0007": "$F$", "MATH_0008": "$F'$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Delta' : F' \\to F' \\times F'$", "MATH_0010": "$F'$", "MATH_0011": "$F'$", "MATH_0012": "$(\\textit{Noetherian}/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0013": "$F$", "MATH_0014": "$F'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-noetherian}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-canonical-extension}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{section-axioms-functors}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-representable}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{section-axioms-functors}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{proposition-spaces-diagonal-representable}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6c805ff870cd843db33d0cbde98b88773aed8dc08eaab26cc26efa5fc35eec20", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f98e1dba5ddc3610002d841b6187467a3146b49584b9e0237598dd07f593085b", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that the sites <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> have the same\nunderlying category, see discussion in Section <REF_0001>.\nSimilarly the sites <MATH_0003> and\n<MATH_0004> have the same underlying categories.\nBy axioms [0] and [1] the functor <MATH_0005> is a sheaf and\nlimit preserving.\nLet <MATH_0006>\nbe the unique extension of <MATH_0007> which is a sheaf (for the <ACCENT_0001>tale topology)\nand which is limit preserving, see\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nThen <MATH_0008> satisfies axioms [0] and [1] as given in\nSection <REF_0003>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0004> we see that\n<MATH_0009> is representable (by schemes).\nOn the other hand, it is immediately clear that\n<MATH_0010> satisfies axioms [-1], [2], [3], [4], [5] of\nSection <REF_0005>\nas each of these involves only evaluating <MATH_0011> at objects\nof <MATH_0012> and we've assumed the\ncorresponding conditions for <MATH_0013>.\nWhence <MATH_0014> is an algebraic space by\nProposition <REF_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a04b8fa6370773c5de8d23957365c538445155cd97a8f663cebbd7780de5da65", "unit_id": "inventory:artin:0GE7:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:f1e8a9b7f46370e58fec3c951bbedbb33c31183ea7a37fba5f07e6e6c35e8d26", "hash": "sha256:f1e8a9b7f46370e58fec3c951bbedbb33c31183ea7a37fba5f07e6e6c35e8d26", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 192623, "byte_start": 192553, "file": "artin.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:dfbde561bad33cf813ba76398525b89b524ee5b7ba1f93e3ab0e975553985bb6", "line_end": 4910, "line_start": 4909}, "owner_tag": "0GH7", "parent_tag": "0GH7", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0GH7", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{section-contractions}", "TEXTCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTOPEN_0001": "\\section{"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "sourc